ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkf200000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;guLBW-k5eM_QSXo-T0UU-mFpMoMrN__mYoVmWb-AgAwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkr0.6139875000000001ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KkPmlRZcOwQVygOtgx9dS56knS8j0Fbw0l6r-gW_DCMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka3ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;wMFQREU7GgPzg2jW9o4VB-i1NFSpMILyP2GjPNNzrywƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke32000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;HJtr9-0ocG0qIOLqBa8bGdeGL1LkQKfQUfxklxnjo5Yƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke14942ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;nTBi4k0-LfFXj4V_ZBO4-U-BqkAtjKiS7CC97a1WMFgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;CjEdlFR5BUv6MWoDiZSfGm5htqRMNzBo-tTmlnibdscƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka3ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;M2iRzFmCEXD65Ig7WgwIG6cT-e7I9nRBRkhQ2WYoI4Mƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;l103HAI9jtnwlYybHgHQGZnPStE3jJfk9ADcA9A7VJIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky/+{"tool":"submit_revision_request","failureLayer":"writer-model","replayFrom":"writer-model","summary":"Four bounded writer-model defects require repair before publication: a near-duplicate em-dash construction flagged by the deterministic gate; a conflation of two distinct year-over-year box office comparisons into a single misleading range; an unsupported \"without digital effects\" qualifier on the Cyclops practical-effects reference; and a causal inversion in the Matt Damon sentence that reverses what the source actually says. All four are local and repairable in place.","requiredRepairs":["Repair near-duplicate em-dash construction in paragraph 2: the second sentence of that paragraph repeats the same em-dash mid-sentence pattern as the first. Restructure the second sentence to use a different syntactic form.","Correct the conflation of 7%/9% box office figures: the manuscript says the summer box office 'trailed the pre-pandemic 2019 pace by roughly 7 to 9 percent' but the LA Times reports two distinct comparisons â€” up ~7% vs. last year and down ~9% vs. 2019. These are different baselines; presenting them as a single downward range is inaccurate.","Remove the unsupported qualifier 'without digital effects' on the Cyclops reference. The LA Times says Nolan's team used practical effects (puppetry, animatronics, robotics) in Cyclops scenes; it does not say the Cyclops was rendered without digital effects, and in contemporary filmmaking that distinction cannot be inferred.","Correct the Matt Damon causation inversion: the manuscript says Damon's 'involvement contributed to the record debut' but WinterIsComing says the film 'helped to make history for star Matt Damon, becoming the biggest opening ever for the Oscar-winning actor.' The source reports the film set a record FOR Damon; the manuscript inverts this to Damon driving Nolan's record."],"repairTools":[{"tool":"replace_exact_body_text","before":"That total cleared the previous record â€” held by *The Dark Knight Rises* at approximately $249 million worldwide â€” by roughly $15 million, according to [WinterIsComing](https://winteriscoming.net/the-odyssey-officially-made-box-office-history-christopher-nolan) and [Deadline](https://deadline.com/2026/07/box-office-global-the-odyssey-1236996979/). The U.S. and Canada haul came to $124.5 million â€” ahead of Universal's internal estimate of $117 million, per the Los Angeles Times, which described the result as the year's highest-grossing opening weekend for any live-action or R-rated film.","after":"That total cleared the previous record â€” held by *The Dark Knight Rises* at approximately $249 million worldwide â€” by roughly $15 million, according to [WinterIsComing](https://winteriscoming.net/the-odyssey-officially-made-box-office-history-christopher-nolan) and [Deadline](https://deadline.com/2026/07/box-office-global-the-odyssey-1236996979/). The U.S. and Canada haul came to $124.5 million, outpacing Universal's internal estimate of $117 million; the Los Angeles Times described the result as the year's highest-grossing opening weekend for any live-action or R-rated film."},{"tool":"replace_exact_body_text","before":"The broader summer box office still trailed the pre-pandemic 2019 pace by roughly 7 to 9 percent year-to-date, according to the Los Angeles Times","after":"The broader summer box office ran about 7 percent ahead of last year's pace but still trailed pre-pandemic summer 2019 revenue by roughly 9 percent year-to-date, according to the Los Angeles Times"},{"tool":"replace_exact_body_text","before":"The Los Angeles Times reported that Nolan's team employed animatronics, puppetry, a real Viking sailing vessel, and a Cyclops realized without digital effects â€” an approach the paper noted contributed to the film's mystique with audiences.","after":"The Los Angeles Times reported that Nolan's team employed animatronics, puppetry, robotics, and a real Viking sailing vessel â€” including practical effects in the Cyclops sequences â€” in an approach the paper noted contributed to the film's mystique with audiences."},{"tool":"replace_exact_body_text","before":"[WinterIsComing](https://winteriscoming.net/the-odyssey-officially-made-box-office-history-christopher-nolan) noted that Oscar-winning actor Matt Damon's involvement contributed to the record debut.","after":"[WinterIsComing](https://winteriscoming.net/the-odyssey-officially-made-box-office-history-christopher-nolan) noted that the opening also set a career record for star Matt Damon, marking his biggest-ever opening weekend as an actor."}],"report":"## Editorial Report â€” reporting-source-3-for-odyssey-becomes-christopher-nolan-biggest\n\n### Overall Assessment\n\nThe manuscript is substantially sound. Sources are credible (LA Times, Variety, Deadline, Times of India, WinterIsComing), citations are properly embedded in grammatical prose, attribution is maintained throughout, the headline and lede faithfully represent the reported event, and the evidence budget is respected at 734 words. The deterministic gate returns publishable=true with a single warning. However, four bounded writer-model defects require repair before publication.\n\n---\n\n### Defect 1 â€” Near-Duplicate Em-Dash Construction (deterministic gate warning: near-duplicate-proximity)\n\n**Location:** Paragraph 2, sentences 1 and 2.\n\nThe first sentence reads: \"That total cleared the previous record â€” held by *The Dark Knight Rises* at approximately $249 million worldwide â€” by roughly $15 millionâ€¦\" The immediately following sentence reads: \"The U.S. and Canada haul came to $124.5 million â€” ahead of Universal's internal estimate of $117 millionâ€¦\" Both sentences employ the same em-dash mid-sentence interruption pattern within the same paragraph. The gate correctly flags this as near-duplicate-proximity. The repair restructures the second sentence using a semicolon construction while preserving all sourced figures.\n\n**Factual warrant:** All figures in both sentences are supported. The $249 million Dark Knight Rises figure and the $15 million margin are corroborated by WinterIsComing (\"besting The Dark Knight Rises' opening weekend total of $249 million by over $15 million\") and Deadline (\"ahead of Dark Knight Rises ($249M WW)\"). The $124.5 million domestic and $117 million estimate are confirmed by the LA Times.\n\n---\n\n### Defect 2 â€” Conflation of Two Distinct Year-Over-Year Box Office Comparisons (material factual error)\n\n**Location:** Final section (\"Theater Relief and the Competition Ahead\"), first sentence.\n\nThe manuscript states: \"The broader summer box office still trailed the pre-pandemic 2019 pace by roughly 7 to 9 percent year-to-date.\" The LA Times source reports two separate comparisons: summer box office is \"about 7% higher than the same time period last year\" and \"still lags pre-pandemic summer 2019 revenue by about 9%.\" These reference different baselines â€” last year and 2019 â€” and carry opposite signs (+7%, âˆ’9%). The manuscript collapses them into a single downward range against 2019, losing the positive comparison to last year and misrepresenting both figures as a unified declining range. This is a material inaccuracy that mischaracterizes the state of the industry recovery. The repair restores both comparisons with their correct baselines and directions.\n\n---\n\n### Defect 3 â€” Unsupported \"Without Digital Effects\" Qualifier on Cyclops (unsupported gloss)\n\n**Location:** IMAX section, final paragraph.\n\nThe manuscript states: \"a Cyclops realized without digital effects.\" The LA Times source says: \"Nolan's reliance on old-school Hollywood practical effects, such as his use of puppetry, animatronics and robotics in scenes with the Cyclops.\" The source describes which practical techniques were used in Cyclops scenes; it does not state the Cyclops was realized \"without digital effects.\" In contemporary filmmaking, practical and digital compositing routinely coexist; the sourced description does not license an exclusive-practical claim. This is a gloss invented by the writer that exceeds what the source establishes. The repair removes the unsupported qualifier and stays within the sourced description while restoring \"robotics\" that was also dropped.\n\n---\n\n### Defect 4 â€” Matt Damon Causation Inversion (material misstatement of source)\n\n**Location:** \"R-Rated, Unfranchised, and Expensive\" section, final sentence.\n\nThe manuscript states: \"WinterIsComing noted that Oscar-winning actor Matt Damon's involvement contributed to the record debut.\" The WinterIsComing source states: \"The film also helped to make history for star Matt Damon, becoming the biggest opening ever for the Oscar-winning actor.\" The source reports the film established a career record FOR Damon; the manuscript inverts the causal direction, claiming Damon's participation drove Nolan's record. These are materially different propositions. The repair corrects the direction to match the source.\n\n---\n\n### Material Claims Verified Against Witnessed Sources\n\n- **$264.1 million global opening**: Confirmed â€” LA Times, Variety, Deadline, Times of India, WinterIsComing.\n- **$249 million Dark Knight Rises prior record / $15 million margin**: Confirmed â€” WinterIsComing and Deadline.\n- **$124.5 million domestic / $117 million internal estimate**: Confirmed â€” LA Times.\n- **45 markets as Nolan's best opening**: Confirmed â€” WinterIsComing.\n- **France, Italy, Spain, Poland, Netherlands, Brazil territory records**: Confirmed â€” WinterIsComing citing Deadline.\n- **International opening ahead of Oppenheimer**: Confirmed â€” Deadline.\n- **R-rated, nearly three hours, no franchise**: Confirmed â€” Variety.\n- **Production budget $200â€“250 million / most expensive R-rated**: Confirmed â€” LA Times and Times of India.\n- **Homer's epic poem / Syncopy / Emma Thomas producing**: Confirmed â€” LA Times.\n- **Matt Damon as Odysseus, Zendaya as Athena**: Confirmed â€” WinterIsComing.\n- **Casting controversy / conservative commentators**: Confirmed â€” Times of India.\n- **First feature shot entirely on IMAX cameras**: Confirmed â€” LA Times and Times of India.\n- **IMAX screens dedicated for three consecutive weeks**: Confirmed â€” Times of India.\n- **IMAX advance sales nearly doubled prior record**: Confirmed â€” LA Times.\n- **70mm ~4% of gross**: Confirmed â€” LA Times.\n- **Hoyte van Hoytema / August 2024 tests**: Confirmed â€” LA Times.\n- **Rich Gelfond ecosystem quote**: Confirmed â€” LA Times.\n- **Practical effects (puppetry, animatronics, robotics, Viking boat, Cyclops)**: Confirmed â€” LA Times. Unsupported \"without digital effects\" claim removed.\n- **Jim Orr \"delivers on every sort of promise\" quote**: Confirmed â€” LA Times.\n- **95% Rotten Tomatoes**: Confirmed â€” Times of India.\n- **Moana second at $19 million**: Confirmed â€” LA Times and Times of India.\n- **No new competition second weekend**: Confirmed â€” Times of India.\n- **Spider-Man: Brand New Day late July**: Confirmed â€” Times of India and WinterIsComing.\n- **Summer +7% vs. last year / âˆ’9% vs. 2019**: Confirmed â€” LA Times. Manuscript conflated these; repaired.\n\n### Fairness\n\nNo allegations of wrongdoing against any individual or institution. The casting controversy paragraph is attributed to Times of India and accurately characterizes the sourced frame. The Elon Musk quote present in Times of India is not reproduced; the omission is an acceptable editorial choice and does not create a fairness deficit, as the article does not deny or contradict the controversy.\n\n### Pipeline Diagnosis\n\nSources and assignment adequately support the event. All four defects are writer-model in origin: two involve adding words or causal relations not warranted by sources (\"without digital effects\"; Damon's involvement as a driver), one is a syntactic repetition (em-dash pattern), and one misreads two distinct statistical comparisons as a single range. No replay from an earlier layer is required.\n"}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;mTL10Lb6j9oxQu7ZSPeucsHd2vAeMunMYEGmwBqdcogƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx$832f6f63-0b0e-4a99-935a-8f10fee1012cƒdp